  "finding_legacy_etkdg_regression": "chematic_legacy_etkdg (the ONLY arm in this benchmark that calls dg::generate_coords, and therefore the only arm PR #253's issue #185/#252 fix could affect) shows sound: 265->265->248 across v0.11.0->pre-2B->v0.12.0 -- a real, one-directional regression: 0 molecules newly sound, 17 newly unsound, introduced between pre-2B and v0.12.0. All 17 affected molecules already had high bond_violation_rate_15pct (0.57-0.91) and nonzero gross_clash_count at ALL THREE snapshots (i.e. these were already marginal/messy ETKDG-refined geometries, not clean ones that broke) -- PR #253 changed dg::generate_coords's starting geometry, which measurably shifted the ETKDG local-refinement outcome for these already-borderline molecules, net negative on this specific metric for this specific arm. This does NOT affect embed_pipeline_v2 (the production pipeline, which uses distance_geometry_v2, not dg::generate_coords) -- confirmed via source inspection (`grep generate_coords pipeline_v2.rs distance_geometry_v2.rs` finds no call). Scope is limited to the legacy `etkdg::generate_coords_etkdg` entry point and any direct caller of `dg::generate_coords`.",
